This page studies the source-free Einstein–Maxwell Cauchy problem using the real two-form $F$ and its six electric/magnetic field-strength components. It fixes signature $(-,+,+,+)$, the future-normal convention $K(X,Y)=g(\nabla_Xn,Y)$, orientation $\epsilon_{123}=1$, and SI frame variables $e=E/c$, $b=B$; no global potential $A$ is assumed.

[[lem-emg-fieldstrength-positive-symmetric-reduction]] derives the six first-order evolution equations directly from $dF=0$ and $d\star_gF=0$. Its spatial symbol is the symmetric curl block with eigenvalues $0,0,\pm|\xi|,\pm|\xi|$, positive time matrix, and the two Gauss constraints. [[thm-emg-maxwell-gauss-propagation]] transports those constraints by the differential-form identities $d^2F=d^2\star_gF=0$, including the finite regularity needed by the high-Sobolev result.

[[lem-emg-coupled-reduced-einstein-evolution]] checks that this Maxwell block combines with the harmonic Einstein wave block without derivative coupling through the algebraic Maxwell stress. [[thm-emg-einstein-gauge-propagation]] recovers the unreduced Einstein equation from the initial constraints, stress conservation and a local zero-data wave-energy argument. [[thm-emg-local-high-sobolev-electrovacuum]] gives the periodic $H^s$ result for $s\ge5$, its smooth-persistence and gauge-uniqueness claims, and a localized smooth existence clause on general initial slices. [[prop-emg-local-sobolev-stability-continuation]] records the endpoint continuation argument and $H^{s-1}$ stability under fixed compact-state bounds.

[[thm-emg-smooth-local-geometric-uniqueness]] verifies the complete-data local Einstein–Maxwell model against the generic covariant local-development theorem. [[lem-emg-smooth-geometric-causal-research-suppliers]] records the actual causal and Cauchy-surface interfaces used by the local and global arguments. [[thm-emg-sourcefree-smooth-maximal-development]] applies the current smooth GHD quotient theorem only after those local obligations are checked. The original Sbierski result is vacuum-only; the Einstein–Maxwell conclusion is conditional on the locally verified model hypotheses. Maximality is within the smooth globally hyperbolic development class and supplies no geodesic-completeness result.

**Conditional status.** The CP01 item files for the electrovacuum model and data definitions, Maxwell stress identity, Gauss–Codazzi constraints, harmonic initialization, and periodic solver are present on disk, and they are listed in the batch-6 manifest, but remain draft with verification precheck pending. Their actual statements and proofs were inspected; the consumers use their exact interfaces conditionally and remain escalated until those draft proof statuses are resolved. The imported GR existence, Sobolev, local-development and maximal-development items used here are marked published, with precheck pending where recorded in their actual metadata. This is a mathematical Cauchy analysis; it reports no measurements or empirical inference.
